!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Prior to processing, samples in PAXgene Blood RNA tubes from 76 COVID-19 patients and 24 healthy controls were removed from -80C to thaw at room temperature for two hours. The samples were then inverted several times to achieve homogeneity, after which 3 mL aliquots were removed for processing. RNA was extracted from these samples using a modified version of the RNeasy Mini Kit (QIAgen) protocol executed on a QIAcube automated workstation. PAXgene samples comprised of whole blood in PAXgene stabilizing solution were diluted with PBS, then centrifuged at 3,000 x g to pellet precipitated nucleic acids. Pellets were washed with water and again pelleted via centrifugation at 3,000 x g. Pelleted material was resuspended in Buffer RLT (QIAgen). Using the automated QIAcube, samples were then subjected to treatment by Proteinase K and gDNA elimination via columns (QIAgen). Flow-through was mixed with isopropanol and passed over a MinElute (QIAgen) spin column. The column was washed with 80% ethanol and purified nucleic acid was eluted in RNase-free water. Purified RNA was heat denatured at 55° C for 5 minutes, then snap-cooled on ice. RNA was quantitated using a Qubit fluorimeter with the Quant-iT RNA Assay kit (Thermo-Fisher). Samples with an RNA integrity number (RIN) below 7 (BioAnalyzer, Agilent) did not proceed to sequencing, resulting in 62 COVID-19 samples and 24 HC samples for sequencing.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Total RNA samples were depleted of globin RNA using the GLOBINclear kit (Invitrogen) as described by the manufacturer. Globin-depleted RNA was quantified using the Qubit RNA High Sensitivity kit (Life Technologies). 10 ng of globin-depleted RNA was used for rRNA depletion and RNA-seq library preparation using the SMARTer Stranded Total RNA-seq kit v2 Pico Input Mammalian (Takara Bio) following the manufacturer’s protocol. RNA-seq libraries were then quantified using the Qubit dsDNA High Sensitivity kit (Life Technologies) and their quality and size evaluated by a Fragment Analyzer High Sensitivity Small Fragment kit (Agilent Technologies).
!Sample_data_processing = A total of 86 RNA-seq libraries generated above were pooled and sequenced on a NovaSeq 6000 Sequencing System (Illumina) in a pair-ended fasion (2 x 100 cycles). 41 M to 124 M paired-end reads were obtained for each sample. FastQ files were used as input for RNA-Seq data processing. Library prep and sequencing were performed at TBseq (Palo Alto, CA).
!Sample_data_processing = Quality control assessment of the reads was done using FastQC.
!Sample_data_processing = Trimming:  The adapter sequence and 3 bases on the 3’ end of the reads was trimmed using Cutadapt as a commonly used procedure.
!Sample_data_processing = Alignment: Trimmed reads were mapped to a reference genome index generated based on the human genome, GRCh38, and a transcriptome reference, GENCODE v32 primary assembly gtf with the sjdbOverhang option set to 100 (default), using STAR aligner (v2.7.3a).
!Sample_data_processing = Quantitation: Mapped reads were finally quantitated per Ensembl transcript ID as defined in GENCODE v32 annotation. Reads were summed up across Ensembl transcript IDs mapping to Entrez gene IDs on order to compare them readily with other viral data assayed by microarrays (AnnotationDbi from Bioconductor)
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: GRCh38
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: csv count matrix of entrez id X sample, raw counts
!Sample_platform_id = GPL24676
!Sample_contact_name = Yehudit,,Hasin-Brumshtein
!Sample_contact_email = yhasin@inflammatix.com
!Sample_contact_department = Computational Biology
!Sample_contact_institute = Inflammatix
!Sample_contact_address = 863 Mitten Road
!Sample_contact_city = Burlingame
!Sample_contact_state = CA
!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 94010
!Sample_contact_country = USA
!Sample_instrument_model = Illumina NovaSeq 6000
!Sample_library_selection = cDNA
!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic
!Sample_library_strategy = RNA-Seq
!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN15287111
!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = NONE
!Sample_series_id = GSE152641
!Sample_data_row_count = 0
